  "_noreturn": "Callees that never return, so their stack use only changes HOW an already-fatal error presents: Rust panics, and C++ throws (the only catch handlers in the image are libstdc++'s nothrow operator new, so every throw unwinds into std::terminate -> abort).",
  "noreturn": [
    "^core::panicking::",
    "^core::.*::panic",
    "^core::slice::index::.*_fail",
    "^core::option::.*failed",
    "^core::result::unwrap_failed",
    "^_Unwind_",
    "^__cxa_throw",
    "^std::__throw_",
    "^__cxxabiv1::__terminate",
    "^std::terminate",
    "^abort$",
    "^__assert_func$",
    "^esp_system_abort$",
    "^panic_abort$",
    "^esp_panic_handler",
    "^__wrap_esp_panic_handler",
    "^panicHandler$"
  ],
  "_indirect_edges": "Function-pointer calls the disassembly can't resolve: mbedtls's f_send/f_recv are our bio callbacks (netstack_transport.cpp mbedtls_ssl_set_bio); the sensor core's LmI2cOps callbacks (sensor_bus.cpp kOps) and the hub's cycle source (sensor_ffi.rs ops_cycles); the driver VM's I2C intrinsics (fx_vm POLL_BUS -> driver_ffi DrvBus) and its LmDrvHost callbacks (sensor_bus.cpp kDrvHost).",
